      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.2", "U5.4", "U2.35", "U4.19", "U4.20"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U5-Pad2)", "DISP_SDA"],
      "observed": "The netlist includes U5 (74LVC1G34) with input pin 2 on Net-(U5-Pad2) connected to U2 pin 35 (PB14), and output pin 4 on DISP_SDA connected to U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2) and R7. U2 pin 35 is not on DISP_SDA.",
      "expected": "The specification's DISP_SDA net is 'U2 pin 35 (PB14) — R7 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2)'. No buffer is present. I2C SDA is a bidirectional open-drain line and must connect the MCU and display directly (with pull-up), not through a unidirectional push-pull buffer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"DISP_SDA\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"4\") (pintype \"output\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"19\") ...) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"20\") ...) (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"Net-(U5-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"35\") ...) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "DISP_SDA: U2 pin 35 (PB14) — R7 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pins 19/20 (D1/D2)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The I2C SDA line is driven by a push-pull buffer instead of being a bidirectional open-drain bus. The MCU cannot read the display's SDA, and the display cannot pull SDA low without contention. This breaks I2C communication with the OLED display.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an extra 74LVC1G34 buffer (U5) inserted in the OLED display's I2C SDA line, which is not in the specification and breaks the required bidirectional open-drain bus."
}

